+The standard 3D Gaussian Splatting primitive is defined by a center $\mu_i$, a covariance matrix $\Sigma_i$ (parameterized by rotation $R_i$ and scaling $S_i$), opacity $\alpha_i$, and color $c_i$ [G]. The covariance is typically $\Sigma_i = R_i S_i S_i^\top R_i^\top$ [G]. The unnormalized probability density function is:
 $$ G_i(\mathbf{x}) = \alpha_i \exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x} - \mu_i)^\top \Sigma_i^{-1} (\mathbf{x} - \mu_i)\right) $$
 Extensions in this family modify the geometric or orientation parameters to address specific limitations:
